[
    {
        "content": "<p>I propose adding the following class to <code>src/Init/Core.lean</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- `Trans r` means that the binary relation `r` is transitive, that is, `r a b → r b c → r a c`.  -/</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- A transitive relation satisfies `r a b → r b c → r a c`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This would join the existing <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Std.Refl#doc\">docs#Std.Refl</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Std.Symm#doc\">docs#Std.Symm</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Std.Trichotomous#doc\">docs#Std.Trichotomous</a>, etc.</p>\n<p>There is the existing <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Trans#doc\">docs#Trans</a> but it takes in 3 relations and is geared towards <code>calc</code>. Additionally, <code>Trans r r r</code> isn't a <code>Prop</code> because it has <code>max 1</code> in its universe.</p>\n<p>Thoughts?</p>",
        "id": 579326869,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773423988
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd be happy with that. <code>grw</code>/<code>gcongr</code> make use of the version of this class that currently lives in mathlib (<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsTrans#doc\">docs#IsTrans</a>).</p>\n<p>It would be extra nice if the <code>@[trans]</code> attribute would create instances of this class when possible. (This would need to be implemented in batteries though.)</p>",
        "id": 579331733,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773425676
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ooh so this opens up the possibility of upstreaming these great tactics?</p>",
        "id": 579374022,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773447130
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As for <code>@[trans]</code>, can we instead declare the instances and have it use TC-search, without tagging <code>@[trans]</code>? Or is that too slow?</p>",
        "id": 579374031,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773447135
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Opened an RFC issue- <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/12917\">lean4#12917</a>, upvotes welcome! <span aria-label=\"raised hands\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f64c\" role=\"img\" title=\"raised hands\">:raised_hands:</span></p>",
        "id": 579374040,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773447145
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The idea behind the <code>trans</code> tactic is that it can deal with things that take type class assumptions, such as transitivity of <code>RingEquiv</code>. However, the implementation of the <code>trans</code> tactic is a bit of a mess and the tactic hasn't really been stress tested.</p>",
        "id": 579376796,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773449285
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>On upstreaming <code>gcongr </code>/<code>grw</code>, I don't think these will be upstreamed anytime soon. In particular I don't want them to be upstreamed, because that will make it much more difficult for me to make improvements to them.</p>",
        "id": 579376887,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773449381
    }
]